{
  "ruleVersion": 3,
  "about": "Shared test vectors for shared/financial-ids.ts and its Flux Memory port (rule version 3, one pass in two fixed stages: cards and IBANs from the original text, then every other rule from the original text with those numbers as `*` separators). Each row: maskFinancialIdentifiers(input) === expect. Rows where expect equals input must NOT be masked. Every implementation also checks, for every row: the output has the same UTF-8 byte length as the input (T13, M18), a second pass changes nothing (T12, M17; the first pass alone must already mask everything, so this is a check, not a rerun), and (F1) every row whose expect differs from its input passes the fast path. hasFinancialIdentifier lists F2: inputs for which it must be true. G rows: a card of 13 to 19 digits joined by a space or dash to a grouped card (FluxMain fuzz), and numbers a second pass used to reach after the first was masked; each is masked whole on the first pass. V rows (v3): a number that passes the card test is masked after any word, `+`, `#` or `*`, in any grouping of whole digit groups joined by one or two spaces, tabs, dots, slashes or dashes (an IBAN too); a typed `*` is a separator; an account run has no upper digit limit and every sort code or BSB shape in the run is masked; a context word ending in a 1 or 2 letter run opens its window before a digit or `*` too; a routing number is any ABA-valid number starting within 24 characters after the word; a kept prefix (1 or 2 letters starting a token, then `*`) counts as glued.",
